---
import Layout from '~/layouts/main.astro';
import SiteFooter from '~/components/SiteFooter.astro';
import SiteHeader from '~/components/SiteHeader.astro';

const title = 'Privacy Policy — Tackbok';
const description =
  'Learn how Tackbok handles local journal data, optional Google Drive backups, and opt-in analytics.';
const lastUpdated = 'August 10, 2026';
const supportEmail = 'tackbok.support@mehra.dev';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <SiteHeader currentPath="/privacy" />
  <main
    id="main-content"
    class="flex min-h-screen flex-col items-center bg-background p-6 text-foreground sm:p-12 lg:p-24">
    <div class="flex w-full max-w-3xl flex-col gap-8">
      <div>
        <h1 class="mb-4 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <div class="badge badge-outline py-3 text-xs badge-neutral">
          Last updated: {lastUpdated}
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="prose-neutral prose max-w-none space-y-6">
        <p>
          At <strong>Mehra Dot Dev</strong>, we believe in transparency and honesty. We
          hope you will find this privacy policy clear and transparent. Do not hesitate to
          reach out to us at <a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}
            ><strong>{supportEmail}</strong></a
          > if you have any questions.
        </p>

        <h2 class="border-t border-border pt-4 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
          Data Collection &amp; Usage
        </h2>
        <p>
          The <strong>Tackbok</strong> application does not require you to create an account.
          Therefore, we neither store nor have access to your personal entries on our
          servers. Your data is stored and processed locally unless you explicitly enable
          the optional Google Drive backup described below.
        </p>
        <p>
          We obtain your email address only when you explicitly request support via email.
          We use your email strictly to contact you to provide support, feedback, or
          important information.
        </p>
        <p>
          Additionally, Tackbok features a donation system. Donations are processed via
          RevenueCat. When making a donation, you may choose to provide a display name (or
          remain anonymous) and an optional email address. The display name will be shown
          on our public donation leaderboard (where the top 3 donors of the past 90 days
          are highlighted at the top, and all other donors are listed below). If you
          provide an email address, it will be used solely to send you a donation
          acknowledgment and a thank-you note. Your email address will never be publicly
          displayed on the leaderboard.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold tracking-tight">
          Google Drive Backup (Optional)
        </h3>
        <p>
          Tackbok offers an optional feature that allows you to securely back up and sync
          your journal entries across devices using your own <strong>Google Drive</strong> account.
          If you choose to enable this feature, the application will request access to your
          Google Drive strictly to upload and retrieve your backup files.
        </p>
        <p>
          We want to be absolutely clear: <strong
            >we (the developers) do not have any access to your Google Drive data, your
            journal entries, or your backup files.</strong
          > All data is transferred directly between your device and your personal Google Drive
          account. We do not store your Google Drive credentials or any journal data on our
          servers, nor do we share your Google user data with any third parties. This integration
          is provided solely for your convenience to keep your data safe.
        </p>
        <p>
          Cloud backup data is protected in transit and by Google Drive. Tackbok does
          <strong> not provide end-to-end encryption for cloud backups in this version</strong>.
          Google supplies the account email so the app can show the full address of the
          connected Google Drive. The selected email is kept beside the credentials in secure
          storage on that device so Tackbok can identify the connected account without fetching
          the address again; on Android it also pins background refresh to that account. It is
          deleted on Disconnect and is never written to a backup, app database, log, diagnostic
          report, or analytics event. Disconnect affects only that device and does not revoke
          Tackbok's Google access for other connected devices.
        </p>

        <h2 class="border-t border-border pt-4 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
          Analytics (Opt-In, Off by Default)
        </h2>
        <p>
          We use <strong>PostHog</strong>, hosted in the <strong>European Union</strong>,
          to understand how the app is used and improve it. Analytics is <strong
            >disabled by default</strong
          >: it only runs after you explicitly opt in, via the Analytics toggle in the
          app's settings. Until you do, the PostHog analytics library is never even loaded
          or initialized and nothing is sent from your device. If you turn the toggle off
          again, data collection stops immediately, any unsent events are deleted, and the
          anonymous identifier is discarded.
        </p>
        <p>
          When enabled, analytics is anonymous. Events are linked only to a randomly
          generated identifier — we never collect your name, your email, or anything you
          write in the app (no journal text, photos, audio, or tag names). Where a number
          could hint at your journal's contents, such as an entry's length or how many
          entries you have, the app reports a coarse range (for example "51–200") instead
          of the exact value.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you turn on the optional cloud backup, it can send a few anonymous
          events of the same kind — for example when a backup starts, finishes, or
          fails. These record only coarse facts, such as which storage provider you
          chose, roughly how long a backup took, and whether it worked. They never
          include your journal text, your photos or recordings, your file names, or
          your email address. The app's privacy screen always shows the complete,
          up-to-date list.
        </p>
        <h2 class="border-t border-border pt-4 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
          Data Sharing and Disclosure
        </h2>
        <p>
          <strong>We do not sell your personal data.</strong> Any data that is transmitted from
          your device to our third-party service providers (such as PostHog or RevenueCat) is
          used strictly to provide, maintain, and improve the app's functionality (e.g., processing
          donations and analyzing app usage). We do not share your information with any third
          parties for their own marketing or advertising purposes.
        </p>
        <p>
          Additionally, the <strong>Tackbok</strong> application is completely ad-free. We do
          not display any advertisements within the app, nor do we collect data to build advertising
          profiles.
        </p>

        <h2 class="border-t border-border pt-4 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
          Third-Party Services
        </h2>
        <p>We currently use the following third-party services for our app:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>PostHog</strong>: This service helps us collect and analyze
            anonymized, opt-in usage data to improve our app (see the Analytics section
            above). For more information, please view the <a
              href="https://posthog.com/privacy"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="underline underline-offset-4">PostHog Privacy Policy</a
            >.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>RevenueCat</strong>: This service manages and processes in-app
            purchases and donations. For more information, please view the <a
              href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="underline underline-offset-4">RevenueCat Privacy Policy</a
            >.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Google Drive (Optional)</strong>: If you enable cloud backups, the app
            interacts with the Google Drive API to securely store and retrieve your data
            on your personal Google account. For more information, please view the <a
              href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="underline underline-offset-4">Google Privacy Policy</a
            >.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="border-t border-border pt-4 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
          Changes to This Policy
        </h2>
        <p>
          We reserve the right, at our sole discretion, to modify or replace this Privacy
          Policy at any time. Any changes we may make to our privacy policy in the future
          will be posted on this page. You are advised to check this page from time to
          time and take note of any changes.
        </p>

        <h2 class="border-t border-border pt-4 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
          Contact Us
        </h2>
        <p>
          If you have any questions regarding privacy while using the Application, or have
          questions about our practices, please contact us via email at <a
            href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}><strong>{supportEmail}</strong></a
          >.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</Layout>
